NAME
    profile - rank emulated routines by exclusive instruction count

SYNOPSIS
    profile on
    profile off
    profile clear
    profile top [<n>]
    profile <cpu> on|off|clear|top [<n>]

DESCRIPTION
    Charges every executed instruction to the innermost routine currently
    on the inferred call stack (exclusive counts, not inclusive) and ranks
    routines by instruction count alongside call count. Instructions
    executed with an empty tracked call stack are charged to
    '(outside any recorded call)'; run 'bt reset' first if the stack has
    drifted (see bt(1)).

    Prefixing a processor name from cpus(1) profiles that processor,
    provided the processor advertises a call stack ('bt' in cpus(1), such
    as main CPU and SA-1 on SNES).

    'profile' measures emulated guest code inside the game. For host-side
    emulator performance counters and CPU profiling, use hwcount(1) or
    Linux perf.

OPTIONS
    on
        Start charging executed instructions to active routines.

    off
        Stop profiling while retaining collected counts for 'top'.

    clear
        Reset all instruction and call counts to zero while staying armed.

    top [<n>]
        Print the <n> hottest routines (default 20), resolved through
        label(1).

EXAMPLES
    profile on
    profile top 10
    profile off
    profile sa1 top 10

EXIT STATUS
    0   Command completed (or usage message printed).
    1   No target attached, processor has no call stack, invalid argument,
        or session service fault.

SEE ALSO
    cpus(1), bt(1), counters(1), cov(1), label(1), hwcount(1)
